{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.MilnorCarriesOrderNotMagnitude","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorCarriesOrderNotMagnitude","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Abs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorCarriesOrderNotMagnitude.not_geometric_order_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorCarriesOrderNotMagnitude.not_geometric_order_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorCarriesOrderNotMagnitude.lean#L101-L105","doc":"The measurement's shape, stated without the numerals: `b₂`, `b₃`, `b₄` all\npositive with `b₃² < b₂·b₄` is enough to fire `not_geometric_order`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorCarriesOrderNotMagnitude.not_geometric_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorCarriesOrderNotMagnitude.not_geometric_order","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorCarriesOrderNotMagnitude.lean#L91-L99","doc":"**The falsifiable form.** A measured `b₃² ≠ b₂·b₄` refutes the single-coupling\norder law, whatever the coupling is — `g` never appears in the hypothesis.\n\nAME2020 gives `b₃² = 2.034` against `b₂·b₄ = 20.56` (isospin-averaged), so the\nphysical cumulants are not of this shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorCarriesOrderNotMagnitude.geometric_order_forces_square_signed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorCarriesOrderNotMagnitude.geometric_order_forces_square_signed","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorCarriesOrderNotMagnitude.lean#L82-L89","doc":"The same with an overall sign on each term, since `μ̄ = ±1`: squaring kills\n`s₃`, and the right-hand side needs `s₂s₄ = 1`. Stated for the aligned case,\nwhich is the one the measurement refutes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorCarriesOrderNotMagnitude.geometric_order_forces_square","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorCarriesOrderNotMagnitude.geometric_order_forces_square","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorCarriesOrderNotMagnitude.lean#L73-L80","doc":"**The order law forces a square relation.** If `b₂ = s₂g²`, `b₃ = s₃g⁴`,\n`b₄ = s₄g⁶` with every `sᵢ = ±1` and the signs aligned so the products agree,\nthen `b₃² = b₂·b₄` — the coupling `g` is eliminated entirely, so the test needs\nno knowledge of it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MilnorCarriesOrderNotMagnitude.muBar_no_magnitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MilnorCarriesOrderNotMagnitude.muBar_no_magnitude","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MilnorCarriesOrderNotMagnitude.lean#L67-L71","doc":"**A `±1`-valued invariant carries no magnitude.** If the `A`-body term is\n`c` times a Milnor invariant normalised to `±1`, the whole size is `c`'s. ","signatureChunk":0}]}